Often called "hex signs," these colorful star murals adorn barns throughout Pennsylvania Dutch country. But while these symbols may now be associated with the region's folk magic tradition they were never originally part of the rituals, says Patrick Donmoyer of the Pennsylvania German Cultural Heritage Center.
Braucherei followers have passed down their rituals and charms in relative secrecy for hundreds of years. But as social media fuels a revival, adherents are grappling with how to retain its soul.&nbsp;
Alice Miller kept her business to herself. It was the 1920s, and even though the Great War was over, anti-German hysteria still swept America. As a Pennsylvania German she already had enough skeptical eyes on her, waiting for any misstep to prove lack of allegiance to the United States…

